{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "7dfd5630-dfb7-8496-bd1d-aac6c6030f41",
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T19:35:48-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Fatima Raposo",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:05-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Lorraine. City Hall's closed for the day, so you've got the after-hours line. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:15-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Lorraine. Well, I figured if I got a person, it's my lucky night. Um, I know it's after hours, I'm calling on the storm line because I didn't want to wait till morning. It's about the drain in front of my place."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:33-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I can take that down. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:38-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "375 Callender Avenue, in the North End. Actually I'm a neighbor, I'm across from the corner there, but the drain is right in front of 375."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:49-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 375 Callender Avenue, North End. And what's it doing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:31:54-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's not taking any water. Since the rain Friday into Saturday, three days ago now, the street in front of the house turned into a pond. It's still sitting there. Cars come through and they're throwing wakes, like boats, right up onto the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:32:12-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wow, so it's still standing three days later. Is the water covering the whole width of the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:32:20-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Most of it, yeah. Cars slow down some, but a couple of them don't. [pause] Sorry, that buzzing is me, I'm at the shop. I cut hair, and my coworker's got the clippers going behind me. Hang on, let me step toward the back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:32:38-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:32:41-04:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's better. So what's got me nervous is the kids. They walk down that way to the bus and to the park, and there's people with dogs all day. Somebody's going to get soaked or slip in it, or a kid is going to splash right at the curb when a car comes by."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:33:04-04:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That makes sense. So the concern is pedestrians, kids and dog walkers, close to the water and the traffic. Let me read back what I have. Storm drain at 375 Callender Avenue, not draining since the Friday-Saturday rain, water across most of the road, cars throwing wakes. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:33:24-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it exactly. And what I'm asking is for somebody to come clean out the drain. I think it's packed with leaves and junk from the winter. I can see a bunch of it stuck on the grate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:33:40-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good detail, I'll put that in. Leaves and debris on the grate. Is there anything else blocking it, like snow or ice piled up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:33:50-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, the snow's gone. It's just the muck. Oh, and there's a little more water down by the other end of the block too, but that one's draining slowly, I'm not worried about that one. It's the one at 375."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:34:07-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, so the main problem is 375 and the other end is just slow. Is the water getting near any houses or driveways?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:34:17-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's up to the edge of the driveway at 375. Not in the house as far as I know. I didn't want to wait till it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:34:29-04:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I'll send this over as a drain cleaning request, marked for the water in the roadway. Crews are working through a lot of requests after that rain, so it may take a few days, but I'll note the safety concern with the kids and the traffic."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:34:48-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I appreciate that. Should I put out a cone or something in the meantime? I've got an orange one in the shop."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:34:58-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd stay out of the road, honestly. Better to keep yourself on the sidewalk and let the crew handle it. If the water starts coming toward a house, or a car gets stuck, call back right away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:14-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, I'll keep an eye on it. Do you need a number for me in case they have to reach somebody?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:23-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. What's a good callback number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:27-04:00",
      "duration": 1,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0173."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:28-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0173, and the name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:31-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fatima Raposo. R-A-P-O-S-O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:33-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fatima Raposo, R-A-P-O-S-O. All set, you're in the system for the drain at 375 Callender Avenue."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:40-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. Thanks, Lorraine. Have a good night."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T19:35:44-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too, Fatima. Stay dry out there."
    }
  ],
